From 67f8c8c0004d1f6aae97b35034bef54a2e8879e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:01:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: kaanapali: keep the display clocks out of the
 unused sweep

The bootloader leaves the panel running. Without clk_ignore_unused the
unused-clock sweep (late_initcall_sync) runs before the msm module has
claimed the display clocks, cuts them under that display, and the panel
stays black after msm takes over (DSI commands still work, modetest
shows nothing). Mark every dispcc clock and GCC's display bus clocks
CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, so the display is handed over intact while the rest
of the SoC's unused clocks are switched off.

A built-in msm claiming its clocks before the sweep would be the cleaner
fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
